{
  "id": "halden-emergency",
  "title": "Halden dispatch: medical, police, fire",
  "description": "A fictional 30-minute emergency dispatch exercise in Halden, for one dispatcher or two side by side. Calls keep coming: falls, chest pain and a cardiac arrest for four road ambulances and an air ambulance; crashes, a fight and a break-in for three patrol cars; kitchen, grass, shed and car fires for two fire engines, one of which carries too little water for a building fire. Three moments test the desk: a twisted ankle and chest pain arrive together, the Torget fight needs two patrol cars while one is on its way to a fallen tree, and a car catches fire beside the kitchen fire Engine 1 is about to finish. Places, calls, crews and timings are invented for the exercise and make no claim about real services. How to play: tap a call to see its suggested unit, then tap the suggestion to dispatch it; a divert asks you to confirm. Or tap one of your units to highlight it, then tap a call on the map; a busy unit offers Do now or Add to end, or only Add to end once it is on scene. The + on a unit adds the next call you tap to the end of its job chain. With two dispatchers, each opens the groups dialog from the role chip and picks the Ambulance desk or the Police and fire desk.",
  "objectives": [
    "Get a unit on scene at every top-priority (P1) call within 8 minutes of the call.",
    "Get a fire engine to the guest harbour car fire within 4 minutes of the call.",
    "Get a unit on scene at every P2 call within 12 minutes of the call."
  ],
